WEBVTT

00:00.192 --> 00:02.353
&lt;i>Previously on&lt;/i>
Two and a Half Men...

00:02.453 --> 00:03.653
&lt;i>Oh, Charlie.&lt;/i>

00:03.654 --> 00:07.324
I would have given anything
to be like you.

00:07.325 --> 00:09.326
Even for a day.

00:09.327 --> 00:10.694
I'm Melanie.

00:10.695 --> 00:12.629
Nice to meet you, Melanie.

00:12.630 --> 00:14.498
I'm...

00:14.499 --> 00:16.533
Charlie.

00:16.534 --> 00:18.135
Charlie Harper.

00:19.704 --> 00:20.837
Whoa. Look who's getting busy.

00:21.112 --> 00:22.580
Hey.

00:23.999 --> 00:25.800
He's acting like
my Uncle Charlie.

00:25.802 --> 00:28.252
He's even dressing
like my Uncle Charlie.

00:28.254 --> 00:30.254
People are really
worried about you.

00:30.256 --> 00:31.789
The only reason people
are worried about me

00:31.791 --> 00:34.258
is 'cause they can't wrap their
heads around how cool I am.

00:35.143 --> 00:37.228
- I'm fine.
- What's your name?

00:37.230 --> 00:39.964
- Charlie Harper.
- You're not fine.

00:39.966 --> 00:42.316
I've got a great idea.

00:42.318 --> 00:44.318
You and me, Vegas.

00:44.320 --> 00:45.803
This doesn't look
like the Bellagio.

00:45.805 --> 00:47.605
Uh, it's the, uh, back entrance.

00:47.607 --> 00:48.656
Hello, Mr. Harper.

00:48.658 --> 00:50.191
If you could,
just come with us.

00:50.193 --> 00:51.525
Uh, don't forget my bags.

00:51.527 --> 00:53.244
And we'll be going
to the presidential suite?

00:53.246 --> 00:54.495
Oh, yes, sir.

00:54.497 --> 00:57.198
Uh, I'm going to need
a bucket of ice,

00:57.200 --> 01:00.201
a bottle of scotch
and two Asian hookers.

01:00.203 --> 01:02.420
Yes. Thanks.

01:04.756 --> 01:06.757
Winning.

01:07.626 --> 01:09.176
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

01:09.178 --> 01:11.161
Here you go,
Mr. Harper.

01:11.163 --> 01:12.663
Now that you're leaving us,

01:12.665 --> 01:15.016
you can have your belt
and shoelaces back.

01:15.018 --> 01:16.183
Oh. Thank you.

01:16.185 --> 01:18.185
But believe me,
there was never any possibility

01:18.187 --> 01:19.503
I was going to hurt myself.

01:19.505 --> 01:21.639
Yeah, well,
it only takes one whack job

01:21.641 --> 01:24.225
hanging from the shower curtain
to ruin it for everybody.

01:24.227 --> 01:26.009
I... I suppose.

01:26.011 --> 01:28.729
And I guess I did lose it
for a little while there.

01:28.731 --> 01:29.780
Lose it?

01:29.782 --> 01:31.816
We had a pool on how
long it would take

01:31.818 --> 01:33.968
to get you toilet
trained again.

01:34.820 --> 01:35.986
Really?

01:35.988 --> 01:37.988
Cost me 50 bucks.

01:37.990 --> 01:40.458
And a pair of nice white shoes.

01:40.460 --> 01:41.575
Sorry.

01:41.577 --> 01:43.544
I tend to leak under pressure.

01:43.546 --> 01:44.578
So you think
you're ready

01:44.580 --> 01:46.047
to go back out
into the world?

01:46.049 --> 01:47.415
Yeah. Yeah, I do.

01:47.417 --> 01:49.583
I mean, I've, uh,
learned a lot about myself

01:49.585 --> 01:51.969
in the last month, and I...
I now have the tools

01:51.971 --> 01:53.421
to deal with life
on life's terms.

01:53.423 --> 01:55.623
You know, a lot of people
say that,

01:55.625 --> 01:58.175
but you'd be surprised
how another couple of weeks

01:58.177 --> 02:00.644
of treatment can make
all the difference in the world.

02:01.480 --> 02:03.264
You have another pool,
don't you?

02:03.266 --> 02:04.381
Nothing personal.

02:04.383 --> 02:05.683
Just trying to get even.

02:05.685 --> 02:07.601
Sorry I couldn't be more help.

02:07.603 --> 02:08.853
That's okay.

02:08.855 --> 02:10.905
Got $100 says you'll be back
before Christmas.

02:11.773 --> 02:13.190
Thanks for your support.

02:13.192 --> 02:16.444
You really want to thank me,
stop taking your medication.

02:16.446 --> 02:17.895
Or double up.

02:17.897 --> 02:20.531
Either way, I'll have
a happy holiday.

02:22.784 --> 02:24.735
Hope you weren't planning
on leaving

02:24.737 --> 02:27.755
before you give
your old buddy Gary a hug.

02:27.757 --> 02:30.073
Of course not.

02:35.013 --> 02:37.098
I love you.

02:42.521 --> 02:45.306
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

02:45.308 --> 02:46.228
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

02:46.229 --> 02:49.429
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 9x09 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Frodo's Headshots&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on November 14, 2011

02:49.430 --> 02:52.630
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

02:52.640 --> 02:53.841
Thanks for picking me up.

02:53.842 --> 02:56.326
No problem.

02:56.328 --> 02:58.678
So you're not
crazy anymore?

02:58.680 --> 03:00.830
I was never
actually crazy.

03:00.832 --> 03:03.350
Then why were you
in the nuthouse?

03:03.352 --> 03:05.969
It's not a nuthouse;
it's a stress clinic.

03:05.971 --> 03:07.053
What's the difference?

03:07.055 --> 03:09.005
About $2,500 a week.

03:09.007 --> 03:11.725
But the good news
is that I got a lot out of it.

03:11.727 --> 03:13.143
I mean, I am ready to deal

03:13.145 --> 03:14.844
with whatever life
throws at me, you know.

03:14.846 --> 03:16.179
Full speed ahead.

03:16.181 --> 03:17.864
Well, that's good, 'cause
I've got something

03:17.866 --> 03:19.449
I want to talk
to you about.

03:19.451 --> 03:21.117
Oh, anything.
Dad's here for you, pal.

03:21.119 --> 03:22.402
Cool.

03:22.404 --> 03:23.853
So remember Megan?

03:23.855 --> 03:25.488
Oh, yeah, that was, uh,
your little girlfriend.

03:25.490 --> 03:26.907
Uh, she's seems
like a great gal.

03:26.909 --> 03:28.191
Well, I'm glad
you like her

03:28.193 --> 03:30.410
'cause she's
kind of pregnant.

03:32.997 --> 03:34.331
Kind of?

03:34.333 --> 03:35.749
She's not showing yet.

03:35.751 --> 03:37.918
She's still in
her first semester.

03:39.553 --> 03:40.971
Oh, my God.

03:40.973 --> 03:42.088
How-how...
how did this happen?

03:42.090 --> 03:44.140
I mean, what about
our talks about, uh,

03:44.142 --> 03:46.643
sexual responsibility
and-and using protection?

03:46.645 --> 03:48.261
I can explain that.

03:48.263 --> 03:49.429
Go ahead.

03:49.431 --> 03:51.147
I was drunk.

03:52.900 --> 03:55.235
Okay. Okay.

03:55.237 --> 03:57.153
I have the tools.

03:57.155 --> 04:00.357
And how do you propose
to take care of this child?

04:00.359 --> 04:01.691
Oh, we got that
figured out.

04:01.693 --> 04:03.893
First, we're going to
quit school and get jobs.

04:03.895 --> 04:05.612
Okay, stop right there.

04:05.614 --> 04:08.248
What jobs?

04:08.250 --> 04:10.566
Advertising-- we're going
to teach the baby to talk

04:10.568 --> 04:12.285
and put him
in E-Trade commercials.

04:13.120 --> 04:14.537
You're joking.

04:14.539 --> 04:18.174
No. We figure the baby they got
is probably getting pretty old.

04:23.381 --> 04:25.048
What does your mother
think about this?

04:25.050 --> 04:26.916
- She doesn't know.
- What?

04:26.918 --> 04:28.351
I was hoping
you'd tell her.

04:28.353 --> 04:30.020
Why do I have to tell her?

04:30.022 --> 04:31.187
Because she already hates you

04:31.189 --> 04:33.306
and she scares the crap
out of me.

04:38.312 --> 04:41.581
Hey, there he is.

04:41.583 --> 04:43.533
Welcome home, buddy.

04:45.536 --> 04:47.454
Thank you.
I'm glad to be here.

04:47.456 --> 04:48.738
Yeah. How you feeling?

04:48.740 --> 04:50.540
Fine. Why are you
whispering?

04:50.542 --> 04:52.542
Oh, I don't want
to startle you.

04:52.544 --> 04:54.577
Walden, I'm okay.

04:54.579 --> 04:56.279
Yeah, sure you are.

04:56.281 --> 04:57.831
Hey, Walden,
guess what.

04:57.833 --> 04:59.582
I'm going to be a dad.

05:01.852 --> 05:03.803
Really?

05:04.689 --> 05:06.923
Wow.

05:07.958 --> 05:09.926
How you feel about
that, Grandpa?

05:11.679 --> 05:14.130
Well, it's, uh, not something
I would have chosen

05:14.132 --> 05:16.232
for him at this stage
of his life,

05:16.234 --> 05:18.818
but he will continue
to have my love and support.

05:18.820 --> 05:22.188
If it's a boy,
we're going to name him Frodo.

05:23.024 --> 05:24.941
You're not making it
easy for me, pal.

05:25.993 --> 05:28.528
You should have
used a condom.

05:28.530 --> 05:31.197
Or you should have.

05:31.199 --> 05:33.867
Hey, look who's back
from the loony bin.

05:33.869 --> 05:36.586
It wasn't a loony bin;
it's a stress clinic.

05:36.588 --> 05:39.155
Did they let you
keep your belt?

05:39.157 --> 05:40.673
Uh, well...
Loony bin.

05:40.675 --> 05:42.792
- There's your mail.
- Thank you.

05:42.794 --> 05:44.260
Hey, Berta,
I'm going to be a dad.

05:46.998 --> 05:48.664
What's funny?

05:48.666 --> 05:50.934
From where you're
standing, nothing.

05:53.387 --> 05:55.021
Did you tell
him your news?

05:55.023 --> 05:56.523
Mmm, it'll keep.

05:56.525 --> 05:57.774
Hey, open your mail.

05:57.776 --> 05:59.692
Okay. Let's see.

05:59.694 --> 06:01.644
Uh, bill, bill, jury duty,

06:01.646 --> 06:02.862
bill.

06:02.864 --> 06:04.013
Ooh! Oh, here we go.

06:04.015 --> 06:05.115
My refund from the IRS.

06:05.117 --> 06:06.232
Ooh.
Whew!

06:06.234 --> 06:08.368
Just in time
what with all these bills.

06:08.370 --> 06:10.737
Might want to set some of that
aside for Frodo's headshots.

06:15.292 --> 06:16.459
Huh.

06:16.461 --> 06:18.694
It's not a refund at all.

06:18.696 --> 06:20.246
I'm being audited.

06:24.635 --> 06:25.585
What's so funny?

06:25.587 --> 06:27.837
From where you're
standing, nothing.

06:32.343 --> 06:33.476
I guess you're
probably wondering

06:33.478 --> 06:35.211
why I asked you guys
to come over.

06:35.213 --> 06:36.479
We understand, Alan.

06:36.481 --> 06:39.382
Mental illness is nothing
to be ashamed of.

06:39.384 --> 06:40.683
I'm not mentally ill.

06:40.685 --> 06:42.218
It was a stress clinic.

06:42.220 --> 06:44.904
Did the door lock from the
inside or the outside?

06:44.906 --> 06:46.389
Uh, uh, well, the... the...

06:49.777 --> 06:52.695
Nevertheless, the reason
I called a family meeting

06:52.697 --> 06:54.030
is because, uh, Jake

06:54.032 --> 06:56.249
and Megan
have some news.

06:56.251 --> 06:57.784
Oh, my God.
She's pregnant.

06:57.786 --> 06:59.085
Well, that was easy.

06:59.087 --> 07:00.620
Who wants cake?

07:00.622 --> 07:02.505
How could you do this?

07:02.507 --> 07:04.541
She made me.

07:04.543 --> 07:05.625
What?

07:05.627 --> 07:06.876
Oh, come on.

07:06.878 --> 07:08.761
Between the two of us,
who was a virgin?

07:08.763 --> 07:10.413
Okay, okay.

07:10.415 --> 07:11.431
What's done is done,

07:11.433 --> 07:13.383
but if we can come
together as a family,

07:13.385 --> 07:14.917
we can deal with this
without finger-pointing.

07:14.919 --> 07:15.935
Your father's right.

07:15.937 --> 07:17.887
Let's just calm down
and talk it through.

07:17.889 --> 07:21.141
Is it just me,
or does Herb and Judith's kid

07:21.143 --> 07:23.276
look a lot like Alan?

07:24.761 --> 07:28.314
Well, you know,
there is a slight resemblance.

07:28.316 --> 07:30.283
- Damn it, Jake!
- What the hell is wrong with you?

07:30.285 --> 07:31.651
How could you be
so irresponsible?

07:31.653 --> 07:33.203
I mean, what were you thinking?
What were you thinking?

07:33.205 --> 07:35.121
Did we raise you not to know
any better than this?

07:35.123 --> 07:36.656
What do you have
to say for yourself?

07:36.658 --> 07:38.458
When are you going
to tell him your news?

07:38.460 --> 07:40.793
Ah, I don't want to
make things worse.

07:40.795 --> 07:45.281
See, that's the big difference
between you and me.

07:45.283 --> 07:47.383
And you're a
grandpa now.

07:47.385 --> 07:48.951
Grandpa. Grandpa.

07:48.953 --> 07:50.953
&lt;i>A grandpa and grandma...&lt;/i>

07:53.757 --> 07:54.957
Hey.

07:54.959 --> 07:56.593
Hey. How'd
your audit go?

07:56.595 --> 07:58.645
It wasn't so much an audit

07:58.647 --> 08:02.065
as a brutal prison rape
with a number two pencil.

08:02.067 --> 08:03.566
I'm confused.

08:03.568 --> 08:05.568
Did you like it or not?

08:05.570 --> 08:08.605
They say I owe them $80,000.

08:08.607 --> 08:10.323
So not.

08:10.325 --> 08:12.525
But the good news is,
if they take

08:12.527 --> 08:14.611
everything I own,
they'll only get four.

08:14.613 --> 08:15.612
$4,000?

08:15.614 --> 08:17.330
Four dollars.

08:17.332 --> 08:18.781
But I'm not worried.

08:18.783 --> 08:22.252
Because I have the tools to cope
with whatever life throws at me.

08:23.087 --> 08:25.088
No, you don't.

08:25.090 --> 08:26.923
Alan?

08:26.925 --> 08:28.324
Oh, Lyndsey.

08:28.326 --> 08:30.793
Sweetheart,
are you a sight for sore eyes.

08:30.795 --> 08:33.463
Yeah, it's good to see you, too.

08:33.465 --> 08:35.465
Oh.

08:35.467 --> 08:37.500
Alan, you're home.

08:37.502 --> 08:40.770
Hey, Walden, I think now's
the time to tell him.

08:40.772 --> 08:42.472
Tell me what?

08:43.307 --> 08:45.141
Aw.

08:49.230 --> 08:51.114
What's so funny?

08:51.116 --> 08:54.150
From where I'm standing,
everything.

08:54.152 --> 08:56.452
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:01.312 --> 09:02.912
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:03.931 --> 09:05.882
I'm sorry you had
to find out this way.

09:05.884 --> 09:07.117
Oh. Really? Really?

09:07.119 --> 09:09.386
How would you have liked me
to hear about it?

09:09.388 --> 09:11.004
Twitter? Facebook?
A singing telegram?

09:11.006 --> 09:14.007
♪ Ta-ra-ra boom-dee-ay,
I banged your girl today ♪

09:14.009 --> 09:18.311
♪ 'Cause I'm a billionaire,
I still have all my hair. ♪

09:18.313 --> 09:19.646
I-I understand
that you're upset,

09:19.648 --> 09:21.681
but you have to see this
from our viewpoint.

09:21.683 --> 09:22.932
What's your viewpoint?

09:22.934 --> 09:24.984
The sex is awesome.

09:26.237 --> 09:27.654
It really is.

09:27.656 --> 09:29.239
He's the best
I've ever had.

09:29.241 --> 09:30.973
No, you're the best
I've ever had.

09:30.975 --> 09:31.908
You're
the best I've had.

09:31.910 --> 09:33.159
- No, you.
- No, you.

09:33.161 --> 09:35.111
Stop it! Stop it!
Stop it!

09:35.113 --> 09:36.329
How did this happen?

09:36.331 --> 09:38.782
It was actually
kind of a meet cute.

09:38.784 --> 09:41.284
Uh, Lyndsey came here
to see where you were,

09:41.286 --> 09:42.752
and I told her
where you were,

09:42.754 --> 09:45.505
and then she started
to cry, and...

09:45.507 --> 09:48.491
bippity-boppity-boo,
we're having sex.

09:49.326 --> 09:50.460
Bippity-boppity-boo?

09:50.462 --> 09:52.178
How do you go
from crying to sex?

09:52.180 --> 09:54.681
With him, it was always
the other way around.

09:54.683 --> 09:56.966
Okay, okay, and-and-and what
was the cute part?

09:56.968 --> 09:58.685
Look at him.

09:58.687 --> 10:00.053
No, look at you.

10:00.055 --> 10:01.170
- No, you.
- No, you.

10:01.172 --> 10:04.441
Hey! Hey! I'm still here!

10:04.443 --> 10:06.025
I mean, how-how
could you do this?

10:06.027 --> 10:07.343
How-how could you have an affair

10:07.345 --> 10:09.028
while I'm locked up
in the booby hatch?

10:09.030 --> 10:10.780
I thought it
was a stress clinic.

10:10.782 --> 10:13.817
Everybody knows what it was!

10:13.819 --> 10:16.619
I lost my freaking mind!

10:16.621 --> 10:20.240
But luckily, now I'm better,
so I have the tools

10:20.242 --> 10:23.693
to cope with whatever life
throws at me!

10:25.746 --> 10:28.047
That's great, Alan,
'cause there's one more thing.

10:28.049 --> 10:29.632
Oh, super. Let me have it.

10:29.634 --> 10:31.634
- You need to move out.
- What?!

10:31.636 --> 10:33.219
Come on, it'd be
creepy if you're

10:33.221 --> 10:35.171
downstairs listening
while we're having sex.

10:35.173 --> 10:36.506
Lyndsey doesn't make any noise.

10:36.508 --> 10:37.891
I do now.

10:38.893 --> 10:41.094
Fine. Fine.
Let me just get my things.

10:41.096 --> 10:42.262
Uh, not necessary.

10:42.264 --> 10:43.680
We packed your stuff.

10:43.682 --> 10:46.316
Oh, yeah. It's all in a storage
bin out by the airport.

10:46.318 --> 10:48.985
But don't worry, I took care
of the first month's rent.

10:48.987 --> 10:50.153
Here's the key.

10:50.155 --> 10:51.604
Why, thank you.

10:51.606 --> 10:54.073
You know, I hope someday,
we can look back

10:54.075 --> 10:56.993
at this as friends
and just laugh.

10:56.995 --> 10:58.661
Someday?

10:58.663 --> 11:00.663
Why wait? Let's laugh now.

11:04.503 --> 11:05.835
Okay, I'll go.

11:07.588 --> 11:10.173
That's it!

11:10.175 --> 11:13.042
I am done being a doormat.

11:13.044 --> 11:15.461
I'll show 'em.

11:15.463 --> 11:17.079
I will show 'em all.

11:17.081 --> 11:19.766
They won't have Alan Harper
to kick around anymore.

11:19.768 --> 11:23.353
And they will be sorry.

11:23.355 --> 11:25.972
Apologies will be made,

11:25.974 --> 11:28.691
tears will be wept,

11:28.693 --> 11:30.426
but it's all gonna be too late

11:30.428 --> 11:33.112
'cause I am out of here!

11:33.114 --> 11:35.949
Sleeping the big sleep,
the ol' dirt nap.

11:35.951 --> 11:39.736
Adios, muchachos,
it's the last roundup.

11:47.162 --> 11:49.946
God, check, please.

11:57.120 --> 11:59.889
Perfect.

12:01.308 --> 12:03.292
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:12.136 --> 12:15.021
Hi! Hi, Mom, it's me!

12:15.023 --> 12:16.806
I need a place to stay.

12:16.808 --> 12:19.325
Walden kicked me out
and my car blew up

12:19.327 --> 12:21.778
and I had to hitchhike
over here!

12:21.780 --> 12:23.496
So, solly,

12:23.498 --> 12:25.415
Missy Everyn no home.

12:25.417 --> 12:28.751
Missy Everyn?!

12:28.753 --> 12:29.752
Come on, Mom!

12:29.754 --> 12:30.703
What are you doing?

12:30.705 --> 12:32.205
Let me in!
I'm soaking wet,

12:32.207 --> 12:35.758
and I had to give a truck driver
a happy ending just to get here!

12:35.760 --> 12:39.295
Go away! I call po-rice!

12:39.297 --> 12:42.465
What kind of accent is
that supposed to be?!

12:42.467 --> 12:45.134
Herro? Po-rice?

12:45.136 --> 12:46.936
Clazy man outside.

12:46.938 --> 12:48.972
You come quick!

12:48.974 --> 12:50.556
Fine, fine! I'm leaving!

12:50.558 --> 12:51.808
Thanks a lot!

12:53.227 --> 12:54.527
Rots of ruck!

13:00.784 --> 13:02.869
Unbelievable.

13:02.871 --> 13:06.122
Blindsided by my son...

13:06.124 --> 13:08.458
reamed by the IRS...

13:08.460 --> 13:10.326
rejected by my lover...

13:10.328 --> 13:12.695
betrayed by my friend...

13:12.697 --> 13:16.299
molested by a truck driver...

13:16.301 --> 13:19.035
cast out by my mother...

13:19.037 --> 13:23.256
and rained on by God.

13:23.258 --> 13:25.842
And this isn't even the worst
week of my life.

13:35.269 --> 13:37.186
Oh, come on.

13:42.776 --> 13:45.328
Might as well make myself
comfortable.

13:47.748 --> 13:51.034
Nowhere to go from here.

13:52.903 --> 13:55.004
End of the line.

13:55.739 --> 13:57.674
Rock bottom.

13:57.676 --> 14:01.177
Can a man sink any lower?

14:05.248 --> 14:07.266
Asked and answered.

14:07.268 --> 14:09.185
Pardon me.

14:09.187 --> 14:11.587
Do you happen
to have a flashlight?

14:13.057 --> 14:14.440
Uh, what?

14:14.442 --> 14:16.859
The light in my storage
unit isn't working.

14:16.861 --> 14:17.927
I need a flashlight.

14:17.929 --> 14:20.897
Oh. Uh, yeah, sure. Um...

14:20.899 --> 14:23.399
Yeah, uh... what the hell?

14:23.401 --> 14:25.401
Oh, here you go.

14:25.403 --> 14:26.703
Thank you.

14:26.705 --> 14:28.771
My fur coats all feel alike
in the dark.

14:28.773 --> 14:30.623
Lot of things feel alike
in the dark.

14:30.625 --> 14:33.442
Ooh, you rascal!

14:33.444 --> 14:34.994
Uh, I'm Alan Harper.

14:34.996 --> 14:36.546
Veronica Hastings.

14:36.548 --> 14:37.880
Come here often?

14:37.882 --> 14:40.449
No, but the night is young.

14:40.451 --> 14:42.552
Ooh. Innuendo?

14:42.554 --> 14:44.303
Not usually.

14:44.305 --> 14:46.756
But if you play
your cards right...

14:48.892 --> 14:50.226
Listen, Alan Harper,

14:50.228 --> 14:52.145
I keep some nice wines
in my storage unit.

14:52.147 --> 14:53.563
Can I interest you
in a glass?

14:53.565 --> 14:55.598
I would like that very much.

14:55.600 --> 14:57.016
Don't go away.

14:57.018 --> 14:59.468
There is no chance
of that happening.

15:03.240 --> 15:08.244
You had a plan all along,
didn't you, God?

15:09.813 --> 15:10.980
Alan?

15:10.982 --> 15:13.082
Yes, Lord?

15:13.084 --> 15:14.450
Over here.

15:14.452 --> 15:16.953
Oh! Oh, Herb.

15:16.955 --> 15:18.921
What are you doing here?

15:18.923 --> 15:20.339
I called Walden.

15:20.341 --> 15:22.508
He told me this is where
I might find you.

15:22.510 --> 15:25.678
Oh, well, I, uh, I appreciate
you stopping by,

15:25.680 --> 15:28.714
but I'm not really set up
for entertaining yet.

15:28.716 --> 15:30.299
I didn't just stop by.

15:30.301 --> 15:31.667
I have some news for you.

15:31.669 --> 15:34.387
Really? Good news?

15:34.389 --> 15:36.973
I had a DNA test done on
my daughter Millie.

15:36.975 --> 15:38.941
Oh?

15:38.943 --> 15:40.560
Turns out she's your daughter.

15:40.562 --> 15:43.146
Bad news.

15:43.148 --> 15:45.481
And it's about to get worse.

15:45.483 --> 15:47.533
Oh, come on!

15:47.535 --> 15:48.350
Good-bye, Alan.

15:48.352 --> 15:49.869
Oh, no, Herb, please, please!

15:49.871 --> 15:52.321
I'm about get laid
by Jessica Rabbit!

15:55.358 --> 15:56.709
No, Herb, no!

16:01.466 --> 16:04.634
Oh, thank God
I'm still in the loony bin.

16:05.869 --> 16:08.888
It's a stress clinic.

16:08.890 --> 16:11.974
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

16:16.365 --> 16:17.614
&lt;i>Thanks for picking me up.&lt;/i>

16:17.615 --> 16:18.964
No problem.

16:18.966 --> 16:21.133
I'm surprised Walden let
you take his car.

16:21.135 --> 16:22.268
I know, right?

16:22.270 --> 16:24.620
With my driving record?

16:27.174 --> 16:28.758
I'm really glad
you're feeling better.

16:28.760 --> 16:29.792
You had me worried.

16:29.794 --> 16:33.229
I'm sorry. Didn't mean to.

16:33.231 --> 16:35.264
But everything's fine now.

16:35.266 --> 16:36.849
Good.

16:36.851 --> 16:38.967
Hey, is it too soon
to talk to you

16:38.969 --> 16:40.152
about something important?

16:40.154 --> 16:42.805
You can talk to me
about anything.

16:42.807 --> 16:45.191
I have the tools to cope.

16:45.193 --> 16:47.276
Cool. Remember Megan?

16:47.278 --> 16:50.079
Oh, God...

16:50.081 --> 16:52.448
Well, we've been
going out for a while now

16:52.450 --> 16:53.415
and all of a sudden,
she's saying

16:53.417 --> 16:54.917
she wants to see
other people,

16:54.919 --> 16:58.754
but I want to keep it,
you know, monotonous.

16:58.756 --> 17:01.490
That, that's it?
She's not pregnant?

17:01.492 --> 17:02.875
No, of course not.

17:02.877 --> 17:05.177
I've been stuck at third base
for months.

17:06.798 --> 17:07.847
That's a relief.

17:07.849 --> 17:10.349
For you, maybe.

17:10.351 --> 17:12.885
Anyway, I was just
wondering if you had

17:12.887 --> 17:15.437
some advice on how to keep
a woman from leaving you.

17:21.862 --> 17:23.779
So how was
the food in there?

17:23.781 --> 17:26.982
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

17:28.151 --> 17:30.035
It feels strange
to be back here.

17:30.037 --> 17:31.453
Just to warn you,
things are

17:31.455 --> 17:33.072
a little bit different
than you remember them.

17:33.074 --> 17:33.956
What do you mean?

17:33.958 --> 17:34.940
I promised Walden

17:34.942 --> 17:35.958
I wouldn't tell you.

17:35.960 --> 17:38.244
- Bye.
- Where you going?

17:38.246 --> 17:39.995
I'm gonna take Walden's car
over to Megan's,

17:39.997 --> 17:41.330
see if it helps me
slide into home.

17:41.332 --> 17:43.799
Wear protection!

17:43.801 --> 17:46.201
I'm wearing it now!

17:54.144 --> 17:56.044
Whoa.

17:56.897 --> 17:59.548
Hey, buddy.

17:59.550 --> 18:01.550
How ya doing?

18:01.552 --> 18:04.153
I'm okay.

18:04.155 --> 18:06.405
Good, good, I'm glad.

18:06.407 --> 18:07.389
Walden, you don't have

18:07.391 --> 18:09.024
to talk to me
like a crazy person.

18:09.026 --> 18:11.660
Oh, crazy people
don't talk like this.

18:11.662 --> 18:12.945
Regular people talk
like this when

18:12.947 --> 18:14.530
they're talking
to crazy people.

18:14.532 --> 18:17.449
Fine. Whatever.

18:17.451 --> 18:18.834
I see you finished
redecorating.

18:18.836 --> 18:21.253
Yeah.
What do you think?

18:21.255 --> 18:22.788
Ah, it looks fantastic.

18:22.790 --> 18:24.740
Oh, hey, check this out.

18:26.092 --> 18:29.244
Computer, lights off.

18:30.881 --> 18:33.549
Computer, music on.

18:33.551 --> 18:37.019
♪ ♪

18:40.473 --> 18:42.107
That's awesome.

18:42.109 --> 18:45.694
Yeah, it's the home
of tomorrow.

18:45.696 --> 18:48.314
Except it's today.

18:49.649 --> 18:52.067
Computer, music off.

18:53.037 --> 18:55.437
Okay, let me try.

18:55.439 --> 18:57.373
Uh, computer, lights on.

18:57.375 --> 18:58.824
Oh, no, that won't work.

18:58.826 --> 19:00.042
It's keyed to my voice.

19:00.044 --> 19:03.445
Oh, well, then how do I turn
the lights on and off?

19:06.449 --> 19:07.616
You can't.

19:07.618 --> 19:09.451
Hey, let me show you
the kitchen.

19:09.453 --> 19:13.672
Boy, sure hope I can flush
the toilet.

19:15.058 --> 19:16.141
♪ Ta-da! ♪

19:16.143 --> 19:19.595
Ta-da, indeed.

19:19.597 --> 19:21.263
Oh, hey, check this out.

19:21.265 --> 19:23.599
I connected the refrigerator
to the Internet.

19:24.351 --> 19:27.019
Ice.

19:27.021 --> 19:29.605
Wait for it.

19:32.859 --> 19:34.410
Is that cool or what?

19:34.412 --> 19:36.495
And if I want ice?

19:36.497 --> 19:39.982
You just call me and then
I'll call the refrigerator.

19:41.418 --> 19:43.819
Oh, oh, check this out.

19:43.821 --> 19:47.373
Computer, television on.

19:48.825 --> 19:51.427
- Wow!
- Yeah.

19:51.429 --> 19:53.262
What is it about
a giant TV?

19:53.264 --> 19:56.465
Right? I mean, just looking
at it gives me a chubby.

19:58.301 --> 20:00.769
Welcome home, buddy.

20:00.771 --> 20:04.023
Oh, thanks, Walden,
but you and I both know

20:04.025 --> 20:05.975
this is not my home.

20:05.977 --> 20:07.175
Oh, sure, it is.

20:07.177 --> 20:09.011
No, let me finish.

20:09.013 --> 20:11.280
I had a lot of time
to think while I was away.

20:11.282 --> 20:14.483
At least after I came off
the thorazine.

20:14.485 --> 20:18.454
And I realized that it's one
thing to live off my brother,

20:18.456 --> 20:20.990
but he's gone and...

20:20.992 --> 20:23.859
now his stuff's gone, too.

20:23.861 --> 20:28.747
I really don't belong
here anymore.

20:28.749 --> 20:29.965
So you're moving out?

20:29.967 --> 20:32.167
Oh, no, no! God, no!

20:32.169 --> 20:35.203
I mean, look at
the size of this thing.

20:35.205 --> 20:37.089
No, I just want
you to know that

20:37.091 --> 20:39.391
I'm aware of the
absurdity of our situation.

20:39.393 --> 20:41.310
Bring it in.
Oh...

20:43.646 --> 20:45.514
Computer, music on.

20:45.516 --> 20:48.850
♪ And I will always
love you... ♪

20:50.800 --> 20:52.382
And let me know if you need ice.

20:53.238 --> 20:57.238
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==
